  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Vision**\n\nI am now focused on integrating the \"ULTRA-LUXURY PRODUCT HOUSE\" approach with the editorial luxury-tech style, emphasizing monochrome layouts. The goal is a highly premium aesthetic, using fashion-brand sensibilities and brutal whitespace. This will involve analyzing layouts and typography choices for optimal impact.\n\n\n**Refining the Aesthetic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specific visual cues. My thoughts are gravitating towards a luxury watch brand/industrial design hybrid, channeling Apple, Balenciaga, and Dieter Rams. The goal is crafting a \"craftsman\" rather than \"vendor\" aesthetic. I need to make some specific tweaks, such as adjusting alignments and enlarging the logo in the hero and navbar. Avoiding all the common startup and trendy SaaS clich\303\251s is also important, and opting for simplicity and confidence.\n\n\n**Implementing the Edits**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specific code changes. I\'m focusing on `Navbar.tsx` and `Hero.tsx`, starting with increasing logo sizes in both areas. In the navbar, I\'m adjusting the logo container dimensions and refining navigation link spacing and typography, aiming for a luxury fashion feel. I\'m also sharpening the \"Let\'s Talk\" button with thinner borders. For the hero, I\'m significantly increasing the logo size, removing the rounded border rings for a minimalist style. I\'ll be adjusting typography for sharper headings.\n\n\n**Adjusting Typography and Layout**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on tightening line-heights for a more \"forged\" feel, emphasizing whitespace to amplify this. I\'m making the \"PREMIUM DIGITAL PRODUCT STUDIO\" text microscopic, aiming for a visual refinement, and introducing microscopic orange accents, replacing colored words with tiny dots or lines. I\'ve also removed animations for a more streamlined look. I will be working on `Services.tsx` and `Portfolio.tsx` next.\n\n**Refining Service and Portfolio Sections**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the `Services.tsx` section. My intention is to embrace brutal whitespace, eliminate boxy borders or refine with 1px borders, and reduce icon stroke widths. I plan on refining titles to be smaller. I\'m also changing to `Portfolio.tsx` to remove colorful gradients for monochrome layouts. I intend to use strict 1px borders and ample padding. I will be adjusting the image styling next.\n\n\n**Updating Contact and Footer**\n\nI am now focusing on the `Contact.tsx` and `Footer.tsx` sections. For the contact page, my vision leans towards a luxury brand aesthetic: large text, precise alignment, and subtle accents. The footer is trending toward a brutalist/minimalist design. Specifically, the \"TRUSTED BY\" section should be very structured, and the images are set to be very desaturated.\n\n\n**Revising Global CSS and Fonts**\n\nI\'m now revising global CSS and fonts, questioning my previous font choices. My thought process is moving towards a structured geometric or neo-grotesque sans-serif, in alignment with a luxury watch brand/industrial design hybrid aesthetic. \"Playfair Display\" seems off, given Apple, Balenciaga, and Dieter Rams as influences; these lean toward clean, structured sans-serifs. I\'m targeting a clean, tracking-heavy sans-serif for meta-text and a sharp serif for luxury elements, reflecting a more austere and industrial feel. I\'m focusing on text and orange elements.\n\n\n**Adjusting the Color Palette**\n\nI am now rethinking my font choices, and I want to scale back on the orange. My instinct is moving towards leaning heavily on Inter and potentially adding a more austere serif or sticking with Inter for everything, a la Balenciaga\'s style, but I\'ll see how it looks. I\'m focusing on `/components/Hero.tsx` first.\n\n\n**Refining Header and Color**\n\nI am now focusing on the orange and fonts, revisiting the `/components/Hero.tsx` and other areas. I\'ve been aiming for monochrome layouts but am now considering a darker or more restrained orange. I\'m reviewing font choices again, specifically looking at how to integrate a clean sans-serif like Inter with a sharp serif for high-impact text. I\'m focusing on `/app/globals.css` and `/components/Navbar.tsx` now.\n\n\n**Implementing Navbar Tweaks**\n\nI\'m now implementing updates to the Navbar, as well. I increased the logo size slightly, aiming for more visual impact, and am still testing typography adjustments. I\'ve also integrated an orange dot in the \"Let\'s Talk\" button for added contrast. The goal is to refine this and finalize changes in the Hero section, as well.\n\n\n**Revising Hero Animations**\n\nI\'m now revising the hero animations, specifically the circles behind the logo. My plan is to remove them, focusing instead on optimizing the logo for maximum impact through more refined motion. I\'m also ensuring the animation is smooth, prioritizing a clean, minimalist aesthetic.\n\n\n**Refining Hero Layout**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the hero section. My current focus is refining the logo animation and typography. I\'m experimenting with bolder serif fonts for headings and fine-tuning the tracking for smaller text. I\'m prioritizing clean motion and ensuring the logo retains its prominence within the minimalist design. The goal is to achieve an ultra-luxury feel, emphasizing the minimalist aesthetic.\n\n\n**Revising Hero Text**\n\nI\'m now revising the hero text and have decided to keep the original wording, while converting it to a monochrome style with adjusted typography. I\'ve switched the text to a serif font and optimized the line spacing for a more premium feel, now incorporating a refined text animation. The goal is a highly premium aesthetic.\n\n\n**Optimizing Hero Typography**\n\nI\'m now revising the Hero text. I\'ve chosen to use the original wording, but convert it to a monochrome layout. I\'ve been adjusting the typography to a serif font with optimized line spacing for a premium feel, and am now integrating a refined text animation for impact. My goal is a highly refined aesthetic.\n\n\n"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_MAX_TOKENS
  }
}
