  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have thoroughly refined the application to establish the **Ultra-Luxury Product House** aesthetic, shifting the positioning completely towards \"Digital Craftsmanship\".\n\nHere is the breakdown of the changes crafted:\n\n1. **Monochrome Precision & Brutal Whitespace:** Struck down clich\303\251 colors and excess gradients. The foundational aesthetic is now structured around a warm minimalist base, massive whitespace, and architectural `1px` border lines.\n2. **Microscopic Orange Accents:** The bright orange (`#FF7000`) has been completely stripped out of large fonts and backgrounds. It now functions exclusively as microscopic structural details\342\200\224subtle blips, 6x6 pixel dots, and precise hovers. \n3. **Ultra-Premium Typography:** Swapped generic layouts for an editorial/luxury feel. Utilized highly-tracked microscopic sans-serif typography (`[9px]`/`[10px]` size with `[0.2em]`+ letter spacing) paired seamlessly alongside tightly-tracked massive serif headings (up to `text-[100px]`).\n4. **Enhanced Logo Presence:** \n   - Greatly expanded the main Flame logo size in the Hero Section. It no longer sits inside decorative circles, presenting starkly like a genuine industrial design object.\n   - Scaled up the logo in the Navbar to command more presence without adding clutter.\n5. **Architectural Photography Tone:** The portfolio features black and white and high-contrast monochrome image treatments (`grayscale`, `mix-blend-multiply`) for the luxury tech and industrial vibe. Hovering briefly flashes the images back into their natural states to reward interaction.\n\nThe UI now feels inevitable, highly crafted, and distinctly premium\342\200\224positioned firmly as an upscale digital innovation partner. Let me know if you would like me to adjust any of the meticulous alignments further!"
