  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reintroducing Orange Hues**\n\nI\'m currently focused on re-integrating those favored little orange accents. I\'m aiming to bring them back subtly, keeping the user\'s past feedback in mind. My primary goal is to improve the overall design while also integrating brutalism with our existing UI style, striving for that \"aesthetic and good\" feel.\n\n\n**Analyzing Brutalism Integration**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into brutalism\'s potential within the design. I\'ve broken down brutalism characteristics and related them to our existing UI, considering elements like borders, contrast, typography, and decoration. I\'m thinking about how to integrate its raw feel, and aiming for an \"aesthetic brutalism\" approach that retains our editorial grace. I\'m exploring changing the border color and using the bold orange for accent marks.\n\n\n**Refining Border Styles**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the border colors, evaluating pure black (`#000000`) for that stark brutalist edge. I\'m considering alternatives like `#111111` with reduced opacity, or a lighter grey like `#E5E5E5` for a chicer feel. I am focused on the balance between starkness and editorial grace, particularly for the `--color-wo-border` variable. I\'m thinking of setting it to `#111111`, but that may be too dark.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'m adding those orange accents back, remembering the user\'s feedback. I\'m looking at `#FF7000` or `#FF8A00` for the details. I plan to use these colors in small ways such as rotating stars or hover states. I am refining the Hero component to accommodate these refinements.\n\n\n**Implementing Brutalist Borders**\n\nI\'m now implementing brutalist borders using Tailwind classes, exploring black with 10% opacity, or a slightly darker shade. I\'m focusing on updating the `globals.css` file to utilize these new styles and considering the balance with a more editorial feel. I will also incorporate stark orange elements, using solid blocks and sharp accents, while re-evaluating the Hero component for adjustments.\n\n\n**Adjusting Color Variables**\n\nI\'m now refining the border colors, considering `#111111` with reduced opacity (e.g., `border-wo-text/20`) as a solid starting point. I\'m exploring aesthetic brutalist additions to components, and making a mental list to check if I am matching the uploaded image\'s design (white color aesthetic). I\'m evaluating the UI elements of the design, with a focus on elements such as Navbar, Hero, Services, Portfolio, and Contact, and what brutalist touches would suit. I\'m taking the uploaded image into account and making notes for aesthetic integration.\n\n\n**Interpreting User Image**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on analyzing the user-provided image. The design is clean with a very light background. The navbar features a \"WebOvens\" logo and links with an orange \"Let\'s Talk\" button. The hero section has \"PREMIUM DIGITAL PRODUCT STUDIO\" with a line, and a headline. Key words are in orange serif. The rendered logo is prominent in the hero. I\'m taking notes for aesthetic integration.\n\n\n**Incorporating Services Section**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Services section, focusing on a grid layout with icons and the right arrow button. I\'m aiming for \"Product Strategy,\" \"Web Development,\" \"UI/UX Design,\" and \"Brand Experience\" to fit neatly. I\'m prioritizing a clean, uncluttered visual.\n\n\n**Reintegrating Orange & Refining**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on the user\'s feedback, aiming for a pixel-perfect replica of the provided image while integrating the requested orange. The hero text is a key target, along with the \"Let\'s Talk\" button. I\'ll focus on subtle but impactful orange touches, ensuring the design remains elegant, and will incorporate brutalist principles where appropriate.\n\n\n**Implementing Precise Orange**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on integrating the precise orange accents, aiming for a pixel-perfect replica of the user-provided image. My focus is on the `Navbar.tsx` and `Hero.tsx` components. The navbar will feature the Fire logo, \"WebOvens,\" and the specified menu items, with an orange \"Let\'s Talk\" button. The hero section will display \"PREMIUM DIGITAL PRODUCT STUDIO\" in orange, a line, and the headline \"We Cook Digital Products That Drive Real Impact\" with the word \"Cook\" in orange. I\'m targeting colors such as `#F96015` or `#FF5C00`.\n\n\n**Integrating Hero Section**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the Hero section details. I\'ll include orange text for key elements. There will be the text below the main heading. I will also incorporate a horizontal line with an orange diamond next to \"View Our Work\". I am including the large 3D fire arch on the right, and the vertical \"SCROLL\" in the lower-left. I\'ll add the 4-point star and accompanying text in the lower-right. I\'m taking notes for aesthetics.\n\n\n**Crafting Portfolio Elements**\n\nI\'m now refining `Portfolio.tsx`, incorporating the details from the user\'s image. I\'ll include \"FEATURED WORK\" with an orange line, the large text, \"Explore All Projects\" with a line and an orange diamond, and the three project cards. Each card will have an image, title, category text, and a circular button with an orange right arrow, all within the card.\n\n\n**Replicating the Image Precisely**\n\nI\'m now laser-focused on accurately replicating the provided image, component by component. I\'m prioritizing pixel-perfect accuracy over any additional Brutalist integration. I\'ve broken down each section, including the Hero, Portfolio, and Footer. My goal is a faithful reproduction. I\'m thinking of building this exact replica and only integrating brutalism, if it suits.\n\n\n**Adjusting UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating the navbar, aligning the navigation links and button as shown in the user\'s reference image. I\'ve centered the \"Work,\" \"Services,\" \"About,\" \"Process,\" and \"Insights\" links and added an orange diamond to the \"Let\'s Talk\" button for visual clarity. The background is mostly transparent as per the image.\n\n\n**Integrating Navigation Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating the navbar, and aligning its details as closely as possible to the user\'s image. I\'ve ensured \"WebOvens\" and logo are on the left, with the navigation links and \"Let\'s Talk\" on the right. I\'m taking the transparent background into account, making sure to avoid conflict with the elements below. I am now working on ensuring proper responsiveness.\n\n\n**Integrating Mobile Navigation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the mobile menu implementation. I\'m building it as a full-screen, white overlay, which appears on toggle. The user can see the navigation links in a vertical stack, with \"Let\'s Talk\" as a prominent button. I am implementing this via `motion` and the state variable `isOpen`, to be shown as a full-screen. This is working as expected.\n\n\n**Implementing Mobile Navigation**\n\nI\'m now refining the mobile menu, using motion effects to enhance its display. The white overlay covers the screen and links are stacked vertically for easy access. The \"Let\'s Talk\" button has been redesigned, with a white and orange appearance. I\'m taking the implementation\'s appearance into account to be as close to the desired appearance as possible.\n\n\n**Refining Hero Composition**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the Hero section, integrating the user\'s provided logo to start. I\'m building it component by component, keeping the provided image in mind. I\'m focusing on the overall composition, and will add orange accents and refine the typography for a polished look.\n\n\n**Integrating Hero Content**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided text elements into the hero section, including the \"PREMIUM DIGITAL PRODUCT STUDIO\" label, horizontal line, and main headline with orange highlights. The orange \"Cook\" and \"Impact\" will be a focal point. I\'m taking the layout of these elements into account, aiming for the correct flow. I am focusing on text size and positioning, for an elegant look.\n\n\n**Refining Hero Layout**\n\nI\'m now incorporating the right-side logo showcase. I am focusing on building the faint circles behind the logo as shown, while keeping the responsiveness in mind. I am now incorporating these design details into the overall layout. I\'m making it match the user\'s reference image for a cohesive design.\n\n\n**Implementing Hero Component**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided code block into the Hero section. It outlines the placement of faint circles behind the central logo image. I\'m taking the motion properties into account for their visual effects. I\'m focusing on ensuring these elements are responsive and accurately positioned, and keeping it aligned with the image.\n\n\n**Constructing Services Section**\n\nI\'m now building out the Services section, focusing on a clean and organized grid layout that matches the user\'s image. I\'ll incorporate the \"WHAT WE DO\" header with its orange accents, followed by the four service boxes, complete with their borders. The right arrow icons are now the focal point to ensure an aesthetic design. I am taking the overall layout into consideration, matching the style from the user.\n\n\n**Structuring Services Columns**\n\nI\'m now structuring the Services section grid to match the user\'s image. I\'ve correctly identified the column structure: a narrow left column for \"WHAT WE DO,\" four equal service columns, and a final narrow column for the right arrow. I\'m building this responsive grid. My focus is on the correct layout and responsiveness.\n\n\n**Refining Services Icons**\n\nI\'m now incorporating Lucide icons into the Services section, with a stroke width of 1 to match the design. I\'m using `Rocket`, `Box`, and `< />` for the code icon, with a custom sunburst SVG for \"Brand Experience.\" I\'m also ensuring a clean visual flow and maintaining consistency with the user\'s image.\n\n\n**Finalizing Services Display**\n\nI\'m now putting the final touches on the Services section, ensuring accurate alignment with the uploaded image. I\'ve confirmed proper icon integration and spacing within the columns. The goal is now an pixel-perfect match with the provided reference, optimizing for a consistent visual hierarchy.\n\n\n**Implementing Services Component**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided code block for the Services section. I am building a responsive grid that includes a left-side label and the services grid, which are correctly aligned. I am now applying borders, and ensuring the display is optimal across different screen sizes.\n\n\n**Structuring Portfolio Elements**\n\nI\'m now structuring the portfolio layout, following the user\'s image, and I\'m focusing on text and orange elements. I\'m noting the layout for the header and introductory text that spans the whole first column. I\'m taking the three project cards into consideration and aiming for a clean and efficient design.\n\n\n**Constructing Portfolio Component**\n\nI\'m now building `Portfolio.tsx` with precision, based on the grid structure of the provided image. I\'ve focused on creating three project cards with their corresponding images, titles, and categories, and will integrate the right arrow button for each. The section is highly grid-based. The image\'s details are now the priority, and I will be building towards pixel-perfect accuracy.\n\n\n**Constructing Portfolio Cards**\n\nI\'m now building out each portfolio project card component, making sure to integrate image placeholders. I am taking the image, title, category, and circular button details into consideration, and I will be building the structure and styling for each card to replicate the image. I am focusing on text size and positioning, for aesthetic cohesion.\n\n\n**Refining Portfolio Cards**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the portfolio cards, focusing on the image integration. I\'ve realized the images have different background needs: some require black, and others white. I\'m structuring each card as a square image with a background matching its content, then text in a separate, appropriately colored block. The code block is now integrated for a consistent look. I\'m ensuring this method creates the desired aesthetic.\n\n\n**Standardizing Portfolio Cards**\n\nI\'m now focused on the Portfolio cards. I\'m noting color variations in images: dark vs light. The images have backgrounds, so I\'ve simplified it to a uniform style for the cards, with a consistent background area below the square image. I\'m exploring uniform card appearances, like `bg-[#0A0A0A]` or `bg-[#F2F2F2]`, and ensuring each card looks clean. I\'m thinking of creating a general, beautiful card.\n\n\n**Implementing Portfolio Card Variation**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided portfolio card code, creating cards with flexible background color handling for various image types. I\'ve standardized the card appearance, using `bg-[#0A0A0A]` or `bg-[#F2F2F2]` where needed, and taking the user\'s color scheme into account, to improve design cohesion and adapt to the diverse images provided. I\'m focusing on ensuring uniformity, and this matches the provided image.\n\n\n**Constructing Contact Component**\n\nI\'m now building the `Contact.tsx` component. I\'m structuring a section for contact information, including \"BASED IN INDIA\" with a globe icon. It will feature supporting text and a slogan. I\'m focusing on text size and positioning. The \"Let\'s Talk\" button will be on the right. I\'m taking the layout of these elements into account, aiming for a pixel-perfect match.\n\n\n**Implementing Hero Headline**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided hero headline, carefully structuring its layout. I am taking the specified font, size, and orange text highlights into account. The focus is to make the design match the user\'s reference image for an elegant, polished look. I\'ve taken the existing code as a guideline for this.\n\n\n"
